From 4a300b308100344275f7a6db1809d494c45b5d9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:59:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Solvers of PETSc on a GPU, SNES: remarks of the review

When MFEM computes on a GPU, the Krylov solvers of PETSc of the factory of
linear solvers gave wrong results (one iteration, relative residual close
to one): MFEM 4.10 places the memory of its vectors in the vectors of
PETSc by setting their internal offload mask, and PETSc 3.26 built with
CUDA saw null vectors; the shell preconditioners of MFEM wrap the vectors
of PETSc the same way. Moreover, the vectors of PETSc of the GPU made
PetscFinalize abort the program when freeing the memory pool of PETSc on
the GPU. With a GPU, the solvers and the preconditioners of PETSc now
compute on the host: the matrices are converted to the AIJ format of the
host, the vectors of PETSc of the host are written and read through
their arrays, and the preconditioners of mfem-mgis given to the Krylov
solvers of PETSc are shell preconditioners of mfem-mgis (on the host
too). PETScSolversTest runs on a GPU (one and two processes); the
linear solvers of PETSc of SNES are accepted on a GPU.

SNES, after the independent review: a resolution which SNES stops for a
reason which the convergence test does not give (the length of the step
when the line search fails, ksponly) is only accepted below the
tolerance or the stagnation tolerance, the criterion on the step being
disabled; the failure of the shell preconditioner of the linear solver of
the problem is reset before each application, and only reported when it
is applied once (a Krylov solver of PETSc which it preconditions checks
its own convergence), its transposed application failing; `preonly` is
set in the code, not in the options database (where the methods of SNES
without linear solver left it unread); DiscardLinearSolverFailure also
applies to the Krylov solvers of PETSc; the stagnation window and the
information on the iterations do not count the initial residual nor the
rejected trial steps; the behaviours are integrated at the unknowns of
the tangent operator if their last integration was made elsewhere; the
products by the tangent operator called by PETSc do not let exceptions
through; an invalid option of PETSc is a failure instead of an abort;
the trust region methods are refused with a tangent operator applied
without assembly (they need its transposed product), and the option
snes_convergence_test is refused. Docs: line searches none and secant,
the claims of the docs match the checks of the test.
